POST to this same address, with no body, once:

  d=$(mktemp -d) && (umask 077; curl -sS -X POST "https://${config.host}/auth/link?code=<the code in this address>" -o "$d/brain.json") && echo "$d/brain.json"

A 403 "error code: 1010" is Cloudflare refusing the client before this Brain saw the call, and the link is not
spent: Python's urllib is refused by its User-Agent. Use curl, or send another User-Agent.

The answer is JSON { name, token, methods, until, deploy, unattended }, with "daily" (US dollars a UTC day it may
spend) when the owner set one, and that command keeps it in a file of
mode 600 in a temporary directory without printing it. The link then stops working. Keep the token there, outside
any repository. Send it as "Authorization: Bearer <token>", e.g. $(jq -r .token <that file>). It calls
the methods in \`methods\` and no others, until \`until\` (milliseconds). With "deploy": true in the answer it also
