Brain's Workers. With "unattended": true nothing it deploys waits for the owner, and it calls infra.shell too. /llms.txt says how.
With "unattended": true its calls to the methods that \`methods\` names by a name or a prefix are made as the owner's
own tab. A method that only "*" reaches is not: such a call is refused where the owner's own session is asked for.

When this token names too little, do not work around it: GET https://${config.host}/auth/ask says how to ask the
owner for more.

Then read https://${config.host}/llms.txt, with no Authorization header (a token reaches its methods and no
other address): how to call, and what this Brain is made of.
`)
